{0 workero}

Write Cloudflare Workers in OCaml. workero compiles your program to WebAssembly
with wasm_of_ocaml and provides OCaml interfaces to runtime APIs and Cloudflare
bindings.

Handlers run in direct style. Calls such as [Workero.fetch] wait for their result
while the runtime handles other requests.

{1 Get started}

- {{!page-getting_started}Get started}: create a Worker, run it locally, and deploy it.
- {{!page-template}Starter project}: files, build configuration, and example routes.

{1 Runtime APIs}

Use {{!page-runtime_apis}runtime APIs} to handle HTTP requests, make outgoing
requests, stream data, and run background work.

